    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve memory locality and loop order by reorganizing the loops to process points in a more cache-friendly manner. Specifically, we will focus on reducing the number of times distances are updated and sorted by using blocking techniques.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Reorganized the innermost loops to improve data locality by processing blocks of points together.\",\n    \"Used a temporary array to store distances within each block before updating the main distances array.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/knn.c\",\n      \"content\": \"#include \\\"knn.h\\\"\\n\\n#define BLOCK_SIZE 16\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float distance;\\n    char label;\\n} DistanceLabel;\\n\\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\\n    DistanceLabel * distances = (DistanceLabel *) malloc(sizeof(DistanceLabel) * k);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\\n        distances[i].distance = -1;\\n        distances[i].label = -1;\\n    }\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        Group g = groups[i];\\n        int length = g.length;\\n        Point * points = g.points;\\n        char label = g.label;\\n\\n        for (int j = 0; j < length; j += BLOCK_SIZE) {\\n            int block_end = (j + BLOCK_SIZE > length) ? length : j + BLOCK_SIZE;\\n            DistanceLabel temp_distances[BLOCK_SIZE];\\n\\n            for (int b = j; b < block_end; b++) {\\n                float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, points[b]);\\n                temp_distances[b - j].distance = d;\\n                temp_distances[b - j].label = label;\\n            }\\n\\n            for (int b = 0; b < block_end - j; b++) {\\n                DistanceLabel current = temp_distances[b];\\n                int pos = k - 1;\\n\\n                while (pos >= 0 && (distances[pos].distance == -1 || current.distance < distances[pos].distance)) {\\n                    distances[pos + 1] = distances[pos];\\n                    pos--;\\n                }\\n\\n                if (pos + 1 < k) {\\n                    distances[pos + 1] = current;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    char most_frequent = distances[0].label;\\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\\n    int current_frequency = 1;\\n\\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\\n        if (distances[i].label != distances[i - 1].label) {\\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n                most_frequent = distances[i - 1].label;\\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n            }\\n\\n            current_frequency = 1;\\n        } else {\\n            current_frequency++;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n        most_frequent = distances[k - 1].label;\\n    }\\n\\n    free(distances);\\n    return most_frequent;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\\n    \\n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\\n    }\\n\\n    int k = parse_k();\\n\\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%c\\\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\\n}\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/knn.h\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n\\n#define BLOCK_SIZE 16\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float x;\\n    float y;\\n} Point;\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    char label;\\n    int length;\\n    Point * points;\\n} Group;\\n\\nvoid on_error() {\\n    printf(\\\"Invalid input file.\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n}\\n\\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\\n    int n;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" n_groups=%d \\\", &n) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    return n;\\n}\\n\\nPoint parse_point() {\\n    float x, y;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" (%f ,%f) \\\", &x, &y) != 2)  on_error();\\n\\n    Point point;\\n    point.x = x;\\n    point.y = y;\\n\\n    return point;\\n}\\n\\nGroup parse_next_group() {\\n    char label; \\n    int length;\\n\\n    if (scanf(\\\" label=%c \\\", &label) != 1) on_error();\\n    if (scanf(\\\" length=%d \\\", &length) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    Group group;\\n    group.label = label;\\n    group.length = length;\\n    group.points = (Point *) malloc(sizeof(Point) * length);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\\n        group.points[i] = parse_point();\\n    }\\n\\n    return group;\\n}\\n\\nint parse_k() {\\n    int k;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" k=%d \\\", &k) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    return k;\\n}\\n\\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt (Point a, Point b) {\\n    return ((b.x - a.x) * ((b.x - a.x))) + ((b.y - a.y) * (b.y - a.y));\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Reorganized the innermost loops to improve data locality by processing blocks of points together. Used a temporary array to store distances within each block before updating the main distances array.\"\n}"
  },
